, "Quadrant": "Leaders"}, {"Company": "Jindal Poly Films Ltd.", "Website": "https://jindalpoly.com", "Founded": "1974", "Headquarters": "New Delhi, India", "Continent / Geography": "APAC(India)", "Operational Presence": "India", "Ownership": "Public (B.C. Jindal Group)", "Employees": "1200", "Core Categories": "BOPET films; BOPP films; metallized films; CPP films; thermal lamination films; coated films; non-woven fabrics; labels", "Specialty Focus": "Brand / Marketer; web_confirmed_flex_pack_player", "Key Brands Represented": "Not publicly disclosed", "Retail / E-commerce / Both": "No", "Distribution Type": "Brand / Marketer", "Contact Person": "", "Role": "", "Email": "", "LinkedIn": "https://in.linkedin.com/company/jindalpoly", "Office No.": "", "Country Code": "IN", "Region Code": "APAC", "Summary": "Jindal Poly Films Ltd. — channel participant (seed_file). Verify: Major producer of flexible packaging films.", "Data Sources": "google_ai", "_crawl": {"founded_year": 1974}, "Data Confidence": "High", "Quality Score": "4", "commercial_role": "Brand / Marketer", "verify_confidence": "95", "_evidence_snapshot": {"source": "", "domain": "jindalpoly.com", "data": {"company": {"name": "jindalpoly.com"}, "business": {"products": [], "services": []}, "intel": {"summary": "Menu\n[ [Jindal Poly]][1]\n* [ About Us  ][2]\n  * [ Overview][3]\n  * [ Board of Directors][4]\n  * [ Corporate History][5]\n  * [ Quality][6]\n* [ Sustainability ][7]\n* [ Contact Us ][8]\n* [ Careers  ][9]\n  * [ Careers][10]\n  * [ Current Openings][11]\n* [ Investor Relations ][12]\n[ [Jindal Poly]][13]\n\n\n[SUP][14]\n\n#### Single Use Plastics (SUP)\n\n\"Goods supplied by M/s Jindal Poly Films Ltd. are not to be used in the manufacture in Single Use\nPlastic (SUP) items prohibited under Plastic Waste Management Rules, 2016 as amended.\"\n\n×\n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[...]\n \n[   ][15] [    ][16]\n×\n\n## Jindal Poly Films Limited is a part of the $ 2 billion B.C. Jindal group, which has been offering\n## a wide range of products and solutions for more than 6 decades. The group is involved in diverse\n## businesses including Polyester & Polypropylene films, Power generation, Cold Rolled Steel Strips,\n## Galvanized Sheets, etc.\n\n## Our Affiliates\n* [[jpfl-films-logo]][17]\n* [[jindal-films-logo]][18]\n* [[globalnonwovens]][19]\n* [[jindal photo]][20]\n* [[Universus photo]][21]\n* [[SMI coated]][22]\n\n \n\n### Technology\n\nWe have continuously invested in the Latest technology. All our lines are wide width delivering high\nproductivity and having the lowest average age in the industry.\n\n[[arrow]][23]\n[Home1]\n\n# Quality\n# Process\n\nA deeply embedded quality culture, stringent quality processes and quality labs equipped with state\nof the art checking and testing equipment ensure that we walk the talk when it comes to consistently\ndelivering quality products.\n\n[[arrow]][24]\n[Home2]\n\n### Quality\n\nWe are an ISO 9001:2015 certified company. Our manufacturing facilities are BRC (long form to\nexplore) Certified.\n\nTestimonials from our highly satisfied global customers.\n\n### Sustainability\n* We are working with our valued customers to optimize packaging structures to reduce quantum of\n  plastic materials.\n* Energy is very significant part of film manufacturing. We have embarked on a journey towards\n  energy conservations projects like renewable power (solar) and energy wastage reduction.\n* We are working with world class recycling technology partners to achieve zero wastage.\n\n[[arrow]][25]\n[Home 3]\n* [[manufacturing-icon-home] Technology][26]\n* [[quality-icon-home] Quality][27]\n* [[sustainability-icon-home] Sustainability][28]\n\n \n\n### Other Links\n* [Employee Intranet ][29]\n* [Customer Portal][30]\n* [Contact Us][31]\n* [Sitemap ][32]\n\n### Investor Relations\n* [Corporate Governance and Policies][33]\n* [Stock Info][34]\n  * [NSE][35]\n  * [BSE][36]\n* [Download Reports][37]\n\n© 2026 - All Rights Reserved. Website Designed and Developed by [Sterco Digitex][38]\n\n#### Follow Us On\n* [ ][39]\n* [Home][40]\n* [ About Us][41]\n  * [ Overview][42]\n  * [ Board of Directors][43]\n  * [ Corporate History][44]\n  * [ Quality][45]\n* [ Sustainability][46]\n* [ Contact Us][47]\n* [ Careers][48]\n* [ Investor Relations ][49]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: javascript:void(0)\n[3]: about-us/overview\n[4]: about-us/board-of-directors\n[5]: about-us/corporate-history\n[6]: quality\n[7]: sustainability\n[8]: contact-us\n[9]: javascript:void(0)\n[10]: http://careers.jindalgroup.com/jindalpoly/apply/\n[11]: career\n[12]: /download-reports.aspx?mpgid=13&pgidtrail=19\n[13]: /\n[14]: #\n[15]: #carousel-example-generic\n[16]: #carousel-example-generic\n[17]: http://jpflfilms.com/\n[18]: http://jindalfilms.com/\n[19]: http://www.globalnonwovens.in/\n[20]: http://jindalphoto.com/\n[21]: http://universusphotoimagings.com/\n[22]: https://www.smicoatedproducts.com/\n[23]: \n[24]: \n[25]: \n[26]: #manufacturing\n[27]: #quality\n[28]: #sustainability\n[29]: https://app.hcmengine.com/ESSJindal/login.aspx\n[30]: http://13.234.46.17:8000/sap/bc/gui/sap/its/webgui?sap-client=500\n["}}, "page_text": "Menu [ [Jindal Poly]][1] * [ About Us ][2] * [ Overview][3] * [ Board of Directors][4] * [ Corporate History][5] * [ Quality][6] * [ Sustainability ][7] * [ Contact Us ][8] * [ Careers ][9] * [ Careers][10] * [ Current Openings][11] * [ Investor Relations ][12] [ [Jindal Poly]][13] [SUP][14] #### Single Use Plastics (SUP) \"Goods supplied by M/s Jindal Poly Films Ltd. are not to be used in the manufacture in Single Use Plastic (SUP) items prohibited under Plastic Waste Management Rules, 2016 as amended.\" × [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [...] [ ][15] [ ][16] × ## Jindal Poly Films Limited is a part of the $ 2 billion B.C. Jindal group, which has been offering ## a wide range of products and solutions for more than 6 decades. The group is involved in diverse ## businesses including Polyester & Polypropylene films, Power generation, Cold Rolled Steel Strips, ## Galvanized Sheets, etc. ## Our Affiliates * [[jpfl-films-logo]][17] * [[jindal-films-logo]][18] * [[globalnonwovens]][19] * [[jindal photo]][20] * [[Universus photo]][21] * [[SMI coated]][22] ### Technology We have continuously invested in the Latest technology. All our lines are wide width delivering high productivity and having the lowest average age in the industry. [[arrow]][23] [Home1] # Quality # Process A deeply embedded quality culture, stringent quality processes and quality labs equipped with state of the art checking and testing equipment ensure that we walk the talk when it comes to consistently delivering quality products. [[arrow]][24] [Home2] ### Quality We are an ISO 9001:2015 certified company. Our manufacturing facilities are BRC (long form to explore) Certified. Testimonials from our highly satisfied global customers. ### Sustainability * We are working with our valued customers to optimize packaging structures to reduce quantum of plastic materials. * Energy is very significant part of film manufacturing. We have embarked on a journey towards energy conservations projects like renewable power (solar) and energy wastage reduction. * We are working with world class recycling technology partners to achieve zero wastage. [[arrow]][25] [Home 3] * [[manufacturing-icon-home] Technology][26] * [[quality-icon-home] Quality][27] * [[sustainability-icon-home